From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-taimen: wire the codec's
 second SLIMbus interface

The WCD9341 exposes four SLIMbus interfaces; taimen only wires AIF1
(SLIMBUS_0_RX/TX) for HiFi playback and capture. AIF2 -- the interface
downstream uses for the voice-call path -- is not reachable at all.

Everything needed is already in mainline: q6afe has the SLIMBUS_1 ports,
q6afe-dai has the DAIs and DAPM widgets, and q6routing already exposes
the SLIMBUS_1_RX audio mixer and the SLIMBUS_1_TX mixer. Only the DAI
links were missing.

This does not by itself make a voice call audible. Mainline has no voice
service (no MVM/CVS/CVP) and q6routing exposes only MultiMedia1..8
front-ends, so nothing can route a voice stream to this port from the
application processor. The value is that the port becomes observable: if
the modem drives SLIMBUS_1 autonomously, a capture from "SLIM Voice
Capture" taken during a call will contain the downlink -- which decides
whether a userspace loopback is viable or whether the voice service has
to be implemented.

Unused links are inert, so this costs nothing when no one opens them.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts   | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
index 5839108cbfed..8c9b425015d3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
@@ -129,6 +129,52 @@ codec {
 			};
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * The codec's second SLIMbus interface (AIF2), which downstream
+		 * uses for the voice-call path. Wiring it as an ordinary DAI
+		 * link costs nothing when unused and makes the port reachable:
+		 * mainline already has the SLIMBUS_1 AFE ports, the q6afe DAIs
+		 * and the q6routing mixers -- only the links were missing.
+		 *
+		 * Note this does NOT by itself carry a call. Mainline has no
+		 * voice service (no MVM/CVS/CVP), and q6routing exposes only
+		 * MultiMedia1..8 front-ends, so nothing can route a voice stream
+		 * here from the AP. It exists so the port can be observed: if
+		 * the modem drives SLIMBUS_1 autonomously, a capture from
+		 * "SLIM Voice Capture" during a call will contain audio.
+		 */
+		slim-voice-dai-link {
+			link-name = "SLIM Voice Playback";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6afedai SLIMBUS_1_RX>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&wcd9340 2>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		slim-voicecap-dai-link {
+			link-name = "SLIM Voice Capture";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6afedai SLIMBUS_1_TX>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&wcd9340 3>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		quat-mi2s-dai-link {
 			link-name = "Quaternary MI2S Playback";
 
